--
--  Test Description
--  The purpose of this test is to check the ability of the GEM to automatically 
--  transmit pause frames when bit 11 of the network control register is written 
--  or when the tx_pause input is toggled.  Furthermore, this test checks the 
--  ability of the GEM to automatically transmit pause frames with zero pause 
--  quantum when bit 12 of the network control register is written or when 
--  tx_pause_zero input is set high and tx_pause input is toggled.
--  
--  Functional coverage
--  � Ensures that the transmission of a pause  frame can be initiated by 
--    using both software and hardware control methods.
--  � Ensures that while using the software control method to initiate the 
--    transmission of a pause frame that driving tx_pause_zero high will 
--    not affect the software control method to transmit pause frames.
--  � Ensures that the transmission of a pause frame with zero pause quantum 
--    can be initiated by using both software and hardware control methods.
--  � Ensures that pause frames can be inserted during the transmission of normal frames.
--
--  Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise the GEM for 10 mode operation.
--  2. Initialise the GEM for full-duplex operation.
--  3. Set the specific address register 1 bottom to 0x12345678 and specific 
--     address register 1 top to 0x00001111.
--  4. Set the transmit pause quantum register to 0x00001234.
--  5. Transmit a pause frame that is 64 bytes, the destination address matches
--     pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, the source address matches specific 
--     address register one address 0x0000111112345678, type field = 0x8808, 
--     pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x1234.  
--     Use the software control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame. 
--     (set bit 11 in the network control register) Also, ensure that toggling the 
--     tx_pause_zero pin does not affect the software control method to 
--     initiate transmission of a pause frame.
--  6. Check the statistics registers to ensure the above operation 
--     was carried out properly.
--  7. Transmit two frames.
--  8. Set the transmit pause quantum register to 0x00005555.
--  9. Set the specific address register 1 bottom to 0x55555555 and specific
--     address register 1 top to 0x00005555.
-- 10. Insert a pause frame right after the 2nd frame from step 7 is finished 
--     transmitting. The pause frame is 64 bytes, the destination address 
--     matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, the source address matches 
--     specific address register one address 0x0000555555555555, type field = 0x8808, 
--     pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x5555.  Use the software 
--     control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame. 
--     (set bit 11 in the network control register)
-- 11. Check the statistics registers to ensure the above operation 
--     was carried out properly.
-- 12. Transmit a frame.
-- 13. Set the specific address register 1 bottom to 0xaaaaaaaa and specific 
--     address register 1 top to 0x0000aaaa.
-- 14. Set the transmit pause quantum register to 0x0000aaaa.
-- 15. Insert a pause frame right after the frame from step 9 is finished 
--     transmitting. The pause frame is 64 bytes, the destination address 
--     matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, the source address matches 
--     specific address register one address 0x0000aaaaaaaaaaaa, type field = 0x8808, 
--     pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0xaaaa   Use the hardware 
--     control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame. (toggle the tx_pause pin)
-- 16. Set the specific address register 1 bottom to 0x00000000 and specific 
--     address register 1 top to 0x00000000.
-- 17. Set the transmit pause quantum register to 0x00000000.
-- 18. Transmit a pause frame. 
--     The pause frame is 64 bytes, the destination address matches pause frame address 
--     0x0180C2000001, the source address matches specific address register one address 
--     0x0000000000000000, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time 
--     to be set is 0x0000   Use the hardware control method to initiate transmission 
--     of the pause frame. (toggle the tx_pause pin)
-- 19. Check the statistics registers to ensure the above operation was carried out properly.
-- 20. Set the transmit pause quantum register to 0x00001234.
-- 21. Transmit a pause frame with zero pause quantum. The pause frame is 64 bytes, 
--     the destination address matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, 
--     the source address matches specific address register one address 0x0000000000000000, 
--     type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x0000.  
--     Use the software control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame. 
--     (set bit 12 in the network configuration register)
-- 22. Transmit a pause frame with zero pause quantum. The pause frame is 64 bytes, 
--     the destination address matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, 
--     the source address matches specific address register one address 0x0000000000000000, 
--     type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x0000.   
--     Use the hardware control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame. 
--     (First, set the tx_pause_zero pin high and then toggle the tx_pause pin.)
-- 23. Transmit a pause frame. The pause frame is 64 bytes, the destination address 
--     matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, the source address matches specific 
--     address register one address 0x0000000000000000, type field = 0x8808, 
--     pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x1234.  Use the software 
--     control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame. 
--     (set bit 11 in the network configuration register)
-- 24. Transmit a pause frame. The pause frame is 64 bytes, the destination 
--     address matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, the source address matches 
--     specific address register one address 0x0000111112345678, type field = 0x8808, 
--     pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x1234.  Use the hardware 
--     control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame. 
--     (toggle the tx_pause pin and set the tx_pause_zero pin low)
-- 25. Check the statistics registers to ensure the above operation was carried out properly
-- 26. Transmit a normal frame. Then queue up a pause frame. Once the normal
--     frame is finished tranmsiting the pause frame should be transmitted
--     The pause frame is 64 bytes, the destination address 
--     matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, the source address matches specific 
--     address register one address 0x0000000000000000, type field = 0x8808, 
--     pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x1234.  Use the software 
--     control method to initiate transmission of the pause frame.
-- 27. Check the statistics registers to ensure the above operation was carried out properly
-- ************************************************************************** --


ten_meg_bit  -- 10Mbit/s operation (2.5Mhz tx_clk and rx_clk, 50MHz Pclk and Hclk)

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      88 12345678  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      8C 00001111  -- specific address register 1 top
apbwr      3c 00001234  -- write pause quantum register
apbwr      04 00280003  -- full duplex and 100M

